---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { db } from '../../../lib/data';
import { specLabel, specsByCategory } from '../../../lib/specs';
const cats = [...specsByCategory.keys()].sort();
---
<Base title="Generic specs" description="Brand-independent specifications (screws, bearings, silicone oils) and the branded parts that match them.">
  <div class="crumbs" data-pagefind-ignore><a href="/">Hobbydex</a> / <a href="/rc/">RC cars</a> / Specs</div>
  <h1>Generic specs</h1>
  <p>A spec is the brand-independent version of a part: an M3x10 countersunk hex screw, a 5x10x4 bearing, a 350 cSt silicone oil. Branded parts link to the spec they are equivalent to, so you can find the same part from another brand, or every kit that uses it.</p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Category</th><th class="num">Specs</th><th class="num">Linked parts</th></tr>
    {cats.map((c) => { const ss = specsByCategory.get(c)!; const n = ss.reduce((t, s) => t + (db.partsBySpec.get(s.id)?.length ?? 0), 0); return <tr>
      <td><a href={`/rc/specs/${c}/`}>{specLabel[c] ?? c}</a></td><td class="num">{ss.length}</td><td class="num">{n}</td>
    </tr>; })}
  </table>
  <p>Screw specs follow published <a href="/rc/standards/">standards</a> (ISO 4762, ISO 10642, ...).</p>
</Base>
